sentences.l:
The Master said: “One who has virtue surely has words;
one who has words does not necessarily have virtue;
the humane one surely has courage;
the brave one does not necessarily have humaneness.”

He said: “The whole man of today — why must he be so?
Seeing gain, he thinks of what is right;
seeing danger, he gives up his life;
under an old pledge, he does not forget the words of his ordinary days:
he too can count as a whole man.”

Gongming Jia replied: “Those who told you went too far.
My master speaks only when it is time, and people do not tire of his speaking;
he laughs only when glad, and people do not tire of his laughing;
he takes only when it is right, and people do not tire of his taking.”
The Master said: “Is that so?
How could it be so?”

The Master said: “Zang Wuzhong, using Fang, sought to have an heir set up in Lu;
though he says he did not coerce his lord,
I do not believe it.”

Zilu said: “Duke Huan killed Prince Jiu;
Shao Hu died for him;
Guan Zhong did not die.”
He said: “Was he not short of humaneness?”

Kongzi washed his hair and bathed and went to court,
and informed Duke Ai, saying: “Chen Heng has assassinated his lord;
I ask that he be punished.”

The Master said: “The gentleman's ways are three,
and I am able in none of them:
the humane one does not fret;
the wise one is not led astray;
the brave one does not dread.”

Gongbo Liao denounced Zilu to Jisun.
Zifu Jingbo reported it, saying: “That lord certainly has a mind led astray over Gongbo Liao;
my strength is still able to lay him out in the market or the court.”

The Master said: “The Way about to prevail — it is what is decreed;
the Way about to be cast aside — it is what is decreed.
Gongbo Liao — what could he do about what is decreed?”

Zizhang said: “The Documents say: ‘Gaozong kept the mourning seclusion;
for three years he did not speak.’
What is meant?”

Yuan Rang waited squatting.
The Master said: “Young, and not humble or deferential;
grown, and nothing to be told of him;
old, and not dying — this is a despoiler.”
With his staff he tapped his shin.
